WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:03.590 align:start position:0%
 
welcome  and congratulations to the gsb class of  2020.  welcome also to families and friends  we're so happy to have people join us  from everywhere around the world  this is not the graduation weekend  anyone anticipated  although honestly i don't miss wearing  my academic regalia in the hot sun  but perhaps it's appropriate the class  of 2020 has been  a pioneering class a class that will not  be forgotten at the gsb  and so once again we break new ground  the gsb's first virtual celebration of  graduates  when you arrived i asked you what did  you want to learn  what kind of community did you want to  build what kind of leader did you want  to become  i hope you have at least partial answers  to those questions  i also told you the gsb would be awesome  i hope it was  i told you there would be adversity and  opportunity  none of us foresaw the scale  a global pandemic and a national and  global uprising against racial injustice  the last few months have revealed our  vulnerability  the fragility of human life and the many  ways in which we can inflict harm on one  another  they've revealed our inner dependence  the extent to which we rely on the work  and support  and love of others they've highlighted  challenges that existed before the  pandemic  society to polarized inequities too wide  reservoirs of trust that we need today  were depleted  in government in organizations in  experts  and our fellow citizens which brings me  to you  you are graduating at a momentous time  i'd like to ask the question  what does the world need from you  you are going forth with many advantages  you have stanford degrees  the skills to succeed in any endeavor a  strong network  you've shown your leadership skills at  the gsb you are positioned for  professional success  and i hope you achieve it i also want to  say  don't let that be enough i encourage you  now and as you go through your careers  to think hard about your metrics for  success there will be visible intangible  measures  the money you make your investing track  record the stock price of your company  i hope you'll measure success by the way  you treat others  and the opportunities you create for  them whether that's individually  or by helping to narrow inequities and  bring people together  remember that business is both a  powerful economic force  and a powerful societal force that gives  business leaders great  influence be leaders of business and  leaders for society  i want to finish by quoting to you some  words from former president franklin  delano roosevelt  in 1932 in the depths of the great  depression which was an another  momentous time he spoke  to graduates in atlanta georgia  this is what he said to them still  resonates today  we need enthusiasm imagination and the  ability to face  facts even unpleasant ones bravely we  need to correct by drastic means if  necessary  the faults in our economic system from  which we now suffer  we need the courage of the young yours  is  not the task of making your way in the  world  but the task of remaking the world which  you will find before you  you two are graduating at a time when  it's important to face facts bravely  to correct flaws in our system to  rebuild i know each of you has the  capacity not just to make your way  but to rise high don't leave it at that  help rebuild in the way that raises  others  set yourselves the task of remaking a  better world around you  that's what will set you apart  next we're going to show a video of your  gsb experience which i hope captures how  transformative  and maybe how awesome your time at the  gsb has been  this is not a normal year we've been  looking at each other on screen and  occasionally from a distance of six feet  or more  as you know stanford is a special place  the beauty of the campus the ability to  learn from brilliant faculty the culture  of collaboration and optimism  and most of all the people during your  time at the gsb  you've gone from being a set of  individuals to being a class that's held  together by  bonds that even social distancing cannot  diminish  the pandemic has shown how much the  world needs leaders for society  who make decisions based on data and  reason who act boldly  who demonstrate compassion and inspire  others  you are those leaders we are counting on  you to bring your ideas  your experience and your passion to  whatever you do  and wherever you go  congratulations to the stanford graduate  school of business  class of 2020 i  am so proud of all of you  what you have accomplished is remarkable  you have put yourselves on a journey  towards making a big impact in the world  simply put you are the  absolute best of our future leaders  now i know this is not exactly  the graduation you were all expecting at  the same time  today's adversity makes your class a  truly historic one  and for now congratulations on your  incredible achievement  and welcome to the gsb alumni family  [Music]  this is the end of your time at the gsb  but as orlando just said  it's the beginning of your time as gsb  alumni the next stage of your  relationship with the school and your  classmates  i look forward to the time hopefully  soon when i can welcome you back to  campus  with orlando and your families and  friends for traditional commencement in  the meantime  i'm so proud of what you've accomplished  and what your future holds  you

